        {
          "id": "4.1",
          "type": "open",
          "q": "Find the equation of the circle passing through (1, 0), (0, −6) and (3, 4).",
          "answer": "Let x² + y² + 2gx + 2fy + c = 0.\n(1, 0): 1 + 2g + c = 0 … (1)\n(0, −6): 36 − 12f + c = 0 … (2)\n(3, 4): 25 + 6g + 8f + c = 0 … (3)\n(2) − (1): 35 − 12f − 2g = 0. (3) − (1): 24 + 4g + 8f = 0 ⇒ g = −6 − 2f.\n35 − 12f + 12 + 4f = 0 ⇒ f = 47/8; g = −71/4; c = −1 − 2g = 69/2.\nCircle: 4x² + 4y² − 142x + 47y + 138 = 0.",
          "years": [
            "October 2025"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "4.2",
          "type": "open",
          "q": "Find the equation of the circle through (2, 3) and (−1, 1) whose centre lies on x − 3y − 11 = 0.",
          "answer": "Centre (h, k) with h − 3k = 11.\nEqual distances: (h − 2)² + (k − 3)² = (h + 1)² + (k − 1)² ⇒ −4h − 6k + 13 = 2h − 2k + 2 ⇒ 6h + 4k = 11.\nSolving with h = 11 + 3k: 66 + 18k + 4k = 11 ⇒ k = −5/2, h = 7/2.\nr² = (7/2 − 2)² + (−5/2 − 3)² = 9/4 + 121/4 = 130/4.\nCircle: x² + y² − 7x + 5y − 14 = 0.",
